WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.139 --> 00:00:05.460
Nanami is the dad, that Itadori never had.

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:09.920
I think, out of all the complex and tragic
characters we have met in Jujutsu Kaisen so

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:14.840
far, Nanami Kento is without any doubt the
most complete character.

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:17.980
He has stuff figured out.

00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:22.030
Listening to Nanami is like listening to your
parents or friends, when you don't want to

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:24.910
admit they have a point, but they really do.

00:00:24.910 --> 00:00:30.109
And so interestingly enough, in a world full
of eccentric, powerful and badass characters,

00:00:30.109 --> 00:00:32.780
of all things it's the guy who's most defining
trait is being the normal grown up in the

00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:39.350
room, that is so relatable and, quite rightfully,
enjoys popularity that rivals that of Gojo.

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:42.610
How can that be?

00:00:42.610 --> 00:00:49.550
Now, I'm gonna say right of the bat that of
course, despite his mannerism and appearance,

00:00:49.550 --> 00:00:53.289
there is very little normal about Nanami in
general.

00:00:53.289 --> 00:00:58.539
I mean the guy runs around with a blunt blade
covered in anti-curse charms to basically

00:00:58.539 --> 00:01:00.980
butcher his way through enemies.

00:01:00.980 --> 00:01:09.070
But as you will see, it's exactly this contrast
between the two worlds, the regular one and

00:01:09.070 --> 00:01:13.170
the jujutsu one, that make him such a relatable
and intriguing person.

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:18.750
This 'act' he'a putting on, of being just
a regular tie-wearing office guy in a sightly

00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:23.250
unusual line of work, is a central part of
his identity and moral perspective.

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:25.729
So, why did he run away form the Jujutsu world?

00:01:25.729 --> 00:01:27.670
How did he get so powerful?

00:01:27.670 --> 00:01:33.210
And what makes him one of the most influential
people for Itadori and the story overall?

00:01:33.210 --> 00:01:52.030
This is the story of Nanami Kento.

00:01:52.030 --> 00:01:55.790
First things first, a quick direction of Nanami's
abilities as a Jujutsu-Shi.

00:01:55.790 --> 00:02:01.710
While Nanami's anime is written with the Kanji
for 7 and sea, his name can also be read as

00:02:01.710 --> 00:02:08.690
nana-mi as in 7 and 3, making it a bit of
a pun with his innate 7:3 ratio powers, that

00:02:08.690 --> 00:02:14.260
allows him to divide a target of his choice
with ten lines and forcibly creates weak spots

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:16.480
at the ratio point of seven to three.

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:23.590
While this ability, is without any doubt powerful,
it requires excellent motor coordination,

00:02:23.590 --> 00:02:28.840
that Nanami demonstrates together with fantastic
athleticism and strength.

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:34.260
While not able to form his own domain, as
a Grade 1 sorcerer, he can use black flash,

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:42.060
a powerful application of concentrated cursed
energy.

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:46.990
Most interestingly however, Nanami has created
a binding vow with himself, called overtime,

00:02:46.990 --> 00:02:50.610
that limits the amount of cursed energy he
can utilize during the time he's officially

00:02:50.610 --> 00:02:53.030
on the clock working for Jujutsu High.

00:02:53.030 --> 00:02:57.800
Once he goes beyond his normal shift however,
and overtime hours begin, Nanami's cursed

00:02:57.800 --> 00:03:05.839
energy swells to a great degree, granting
him a significant boost in fighting power.

00:03:05.839 --> 00:03:06.839
-

00:03:06.839 --> 00:03:15.769
While Nanami might not appear to be the most
creative or complex on the surface, you only

00:03:15.769 --> 00:03:21.269
need to go a little bit deeper to find that
in Akutami's net of carefully crafted characters,

00:03:21.269 --> 00:03:26.299
he is one of the most multi-layered and thought-through
personalities in the story.

00:03:26.299 --> 00:03:30.120
This becomes especially clear when we look
at the two main functions of his in the story:

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:36.530
Being a father figure to Itadori and drawing
you dear viewer, deeper into the story.

00:03:36.530 --> 00:03:37.760
Let's start with the latter.

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:42.550
To understand, how what makes Nanami so important
in terms of world building, I want to give

00:03:42.550 --> 00:03:45.290
you a quick overview of the world in Jujutsu
Kaisen.

00:03:45.290 --> 00:03:50.650
Much more so than many other anime, JuJutsu
Kaisen has taken it as a central designing

00:03:50.650 --> 00:03:56.030
principle to integrate this supernatural world
of courses and sorcerers into a real and timely

00:03:56.030 --> 00:03:58.250
depiction of our world.

00:03:58.250 --> 00:04:03.959
As someone living in Tokyo myself, I can attest
to 100% that Akutami has literally taken the

00:04:03.959 --> 00:04:17.150
real modern Japan and integrated his own world
as a hidden hub within it.

00:04:17.150 --> 00:04:21.800
This in itself is nothing new, it's something
we for example also see in Bleach, one of

00:04:21.800 --> 00:04:23.820
the major inspirations for the story.

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:28.370
However, whole Ichigo and co keep jumping
form one world to the next and there rarely

00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:33.180
seem to be references to the real world, in
Jujutsu Kaisen, both sorcerers and Curses

00:04:33.180 --> 00:04:35.410
alike are part of modern life.

00:04:35.410 --> 00:04:41.790
As a result, we see Nobora shopping in Shibuya,
Tojo going to Idol meet-ups, Gojo making Itadori

00:04:41.790 --> 00:04:51.640
watch hours of famous Hollywood movies, Geto
and the curses meeting up in a family restaurant

00:04:51.640 --> 00:04:55.640
and even principal gakuganji, who first is
introduced as the typical old-guy-preserving-traditions-and-following-the-rules-at-any-cost

00:04:55.640 --> 00:05:03.730
type of character, turns out to have powers
that have him use an electric guitar.

00:05:03.730 --> 00:05:10.290
The most eye-catching thing however, might
be the use of smart-phones in the story.

00:05:10.290 --> 00:05:15.600
As the Nerdwriter, one of my favorite YouTubers,
fantastically explains in one of his videos,

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:21.520
the reason, we usually get so few smartphones
in Movies and Shows, is the addictive, time-consuming

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:26.850
and never stopping data mining we constantly
perform on our smartphones.

00:05:26.850 --> 00:05:31.080
Many of us have started to resent the way
these devices control our lives and nourish

00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:41.630
our insecurities 
and fears.

00:05:41.630 --> 00:05:48.550
- Nerdwriter - JuJutsu Kaisen on the other
hand is all about confronting fears and insecurities

00:05:48.550 --> 00:05:54.000
and figuring out what is worth giving our
time and even our lives for.

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:58.140
And I think no other character represents
this better than Nanami.

00:05:58.140 --> 00:06:03.650
He is depicted in a full suit and tie, with
neat haircut - nothing less than salaryman

00:06:03.650 --> 00:06:06.190
image Gojo calls him.

00:06:06.190 --> 00:06:10.850
Without his unique glasses, you won’t be
able to differentiate him from common office

00:06:10.850 --> 00:06:11.850
worker.

00:06:11.850 --> 00:06:16.630
He’s the stiff seriousness formality in
contrast to Gojo’s easy, overly friendly

00:06:16.630 --> 00:06:18.530
and overly informal attitude.

00:06:18.530 --> 00:06:27.020
Even during their first meeting, he demands
a formal introduction from Itadori.

00:06:27.020 --> 00:06:29.450
He's the type of guy that likes following
rules and procedures.

00:06:29.450 --> 00:06:33.910
Nanami's image as the normal guy, who used
to work both as a salary man and a Sorcerer,

00:06:33.910 --> 00:06:38.840
helps us connect to the world of Jujutsu Kaisen,
better than maybe any other character.

00:06:38.840 --> 00:06:47.720
For him, office work is shit -- but so is
being a Jujutsu sorcerer.

00:06:47.720 --> 00:06:52.820
We all can relate that working over-hours
in a boring office job, is not merely boring

00:06:52.820 --> 00:06:55.550
and dissatisfying, it's draining.

00:06:55.550 --> 00:07:00.340
And Nanami basically putting this type of
work and jujutsu on the same level, makes

00:07:00.340 --> 00:07:06.350
the actions of gojo, itadori and co suddenly
a lot more relatable and real as well.

00:07:06.350 --> 00:07:13.330
Yes, being able to do a domain expansion might
be dope, but in the end being a jujutsu sorcerer

00:07:13.330 --> 00:07:21.520
is just as shit a job as working yourself
to death as a salary man.

00:07:21.520 --> 00:07:25.610
-- Just like smartphones, we usually don't
like seeing the unpleasantness of a boring

00:07:25.610 --> 00:07:29.300
and draining job reflected back at us when
watching something.

00:07:29.300 --> 00:07:34.350
And yet JuJutsu Kaisen, uses these elements
consciously to create a realistic vibe, while

00:07:34.350 --> 00:07:39.200
at the same time enforcing the central moral
question of the story: What does it mean to

00:07:39.200 --> 00:07:41.220
live a good life, worth living.

00:07:41.220 --> 00:07:43.970
Nanami is the first character in this series
of character analysis, that has a flat character

00:07:43.970 --> 00:07:49.270
arc, in other words, he knows the truth about
the world, that most other characters have

00:07:49.270 --> 00:07:50.860
to figure out.

00:07:50.860 --> 00:07:54.910
Nanami knows that in general, the world is
mostly shit.

00:07:54.910 --> 00:07:57.570
Jujutsu sucks, doing a normal job sucks.

00:07:57.570 --> 00:08:01.740
In other words, life itself doesn't present
you with a deeper purpose and happiness by

00:08:01.740 --> 00:08:09.930
itself.

00:08:09.930 --> 00:08:14.990
Nanami came to this realization after initially
running away from the terrors associated with

00:08:14.990 --> 00:08:16.370
being a sorcerer.

00:08:16.370 --> 00:08:21.030
Seeing his comrades die and suffer around
him, had a deep impact on Nanami, who, as

00:08:21.030 --> 00:08:26.250
we will discuss in a bit, despite his hard
shell has an incredibly soft core.

00:08:26.250 --> 00:08:31.860
So, he decided to run away, work his ass of
as a salary man and earn enough so he could

00:08:31.860 --> 00:08:38.801
retire early somewhere outside of Japan, away
from the Jujutsu world and all the suffering.

00:08:38.801 --> 00:08:48.680
And yet, the office work drained him just
as much and made him maybe even more unhappy.

00:08:48.680 --> 00:08:52.890
Pointlessly thinking about money the entire
day, while failing to live his life in the

00:08:52.890 --> 00:08:54.200
moment.

00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:58.140
And so, while it might seem like a minor thing
in the context of the story, the two scenes

00:08:58.140 --> 00:09:02.130
of Nanami visiting the bread store are actually
the most defining of his entire character.

00:09:02.130 --> 00:09:06.940
Because as he decides to release the girl
from the burden of the curse on her shoulder

00:09:06.940 --> 00:09:13.760
after all, that neither she nor any doctor
can see, Nanami finally realizes, that while

00:09:13.760 --> 00:09:19.640
life is shit and offers no purpose in itself,
he himself is free to find his own purpose

00:09:19.640 --> 00:09:27.580
and fulfillment in life.

00:09:27.580 --> 00:09:31.800
And while Itadori has only inherited his wish
to help others from his grandpa, and hasn't

00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:37.830
really figure out himself why that matters,
Nanami in this moment understands, that helping

00:09:37.830 --> 00:09:41.320
others is what gives his live meaning.

00:09:41.320 --> 00:09:46.950
While being a Jujutsu-shi might be just as
bad or, considering all the violence and death,

00:09:46.950 --> 00:09:51.130
worse a job than working in an office job,
as a sorcerer he has the rare ability to help

00:09:51.130 --> 00:09:54.390
others who are suffering under the terror
of curses.

00:09:54.390 --> 00:09:57.010
And this conclusion is very important.

00:09:57.010 --> 00:10:01.260
Because someone like Mshito for example also
understands this truth about the world.

00:10:01.260 --> 00:10:06.550
However, as a result to this insight, he decides
to simply live out his desire to fight and

00:10:06.550 --> 00:10:13.680
hurt others.

00:10:13.680 --> 00:10:20.130
As always with flat characters, the most important
thing is how the use their knowledge to influence

00:10:20.130 --> 00:10:23.680
the world, either for the good or bad.

00:10:23.680 --> 00:10:28.590
Now the second major role Nanami plays in
the story is that of the adult in the room

00:10:28.590 --> 00:10:33.270
and ultimately one of the most influential
people on Itadoris development.

00:10:33.270 --> 00:10:38.390
This becomes especially clear when looking
at his relationships with Yuji, Gojo and even

00:10:38.390 --> 00:10:39.390
Mahito.

00:10:39.390 --> 00:10:43.110
All three of them are immature in different
ways.

00:10:43.110 --> 00:10:48.070
Itadori of course literally is a kid, that
has grown up without his parents and as so

00:10:48.070 --> 00:10:52.200
many shounen heroes has been thrown into a
world of violence.

00:10:52.200 --> 00:10:57.440
Mahito is a newly born curse, that like a
child likes to play around and try things

00:10:57.440 --> 00:11:02.880
out, such as testing his own powers or having
out with a human to see what it's like.

00:11:02.880 --> 00:11:08.030
Finally, Gojo himself, who is actually Nanami's
senior, can be quite serious and frightening

00:11:08.030 --> 00:11:17.530
at times, but as I discuss in depth in his
video, is nonetheless emotionally immature.

00:11:17.530 --> 00:11:23.490
And while ironically, all three of them turn
out to be stronger than Nanami, in their interactions

00:11:23.490 --> 00:11:33.400
with him, their immaturity becomes clear.

00:11:33.400 --> 00:11:37.030
Nanami is in many ways an alternative version
of Gojo.

00:11:37.030 --> 00:11:42.890
While the strongest sorcerer is charismatic,
eccentric and un-conformist, Nanami represents

00:11:42.890 --> 00:11:47.900
a sorcerer who follows the rules, sees the
work they do as a job and is fairly reasonable

00:11:47.900 --> 00:11:50.710
and straight laced in his behavior.

00:11:50.710 --> 00:11:55.060
He seems to believe in a higher, external
set of rules and values, that everyone should

00:11:55.060 --> 00:11:56.210
conform to.

00:11:56.210 --> 00:12:01.010
Goodness and righteousness in particular are
two ideals that define his life, and that

00:12:01.010 --> 00:12:04.740
end up shaping him, even if he tries to avoid
then.

00:12:04.740 --> 00:12:09.790
In that sense, Nanami is different from Yuji
or Fushiguro, he doesn't actually want to

00:12:09.790 --> 00:12:16.490
save everyone or even the ones he holds dear,
knowing fully well it's not possible for him.

00:12:16.490 --> 00:12:22.110
And yet whenever he's faced with the option
to help, he does so, holding himself to his

00:12:22.110 --> 00:12:23.920
own high standards.

00:12:23.920 --> 00:12:28.210
All despite not being a very self righteous
person himself.

00:12:28.210 --> 00:12:34.820
Gojo has a high opinion of himself, but low
social skills, and low compliance with others.

00:12:34.820 --> 00:12:38.900
Nanami is his inversion, he has a low opinion
of himself, but he’s geared much more to

00:12:38.900 --> 00:12:45.990
watching over and cooperating with others.

00:12:45.990 --> 00:12:54.670
This results in the disrespect he has for
Gojo and his methods of handling things, but

00:12:54.670 --> 00:13:00.330
goes out of his way to cooperate with him
and not let his personal opinions interfere

00:13:00.330 --> 00:13:01.330
with his work.

00:13:01.330 --> 00:13:05.680
And this difference is reflected perfectly
in their approach to teaching.

00:13:05.680 --> 00:13:10.730
While Gojo is great at bringing Yuji up to
speed in terms of power, basically crash-coursing

00:13:10.730 --> 00:13:16.180
him into being a first class sorcerer in mere
weeks, due to his own character flaw, he can't

00:13:16.180 --> 00:13:19.500
teach Itadori on an emotional and human level.

00:13:19.500 --> 00:13:21.340
This is where Nanami comes in.

00:13:21.340 --> 00:13:28.300
While he doesn't make Yuji any stronger, he
teaches him about morality, duty and in general

00:13:28.300 --> 00:13:31.050
what it means being a part of the Jujutsu
world.

00:13:31.050 --> 00:13:37.020
He also, allows Yuji, who reminds him of his
own time as student, to be a kid, which, even

00:13:37.020 --> 00:13:41.580
though it might annoy him at first, is incredibly
important for dealing with the flaws and struggles

00:13:41.580 --> 00:13:46.470
that come with being a teenager that suddenly
has to make complex moral decisions, like

00:13:46.470 --> 00:13:51.890
taking a human life and that is way to reckless
with his own life already.

00:13:51.890 --> 00:13:56.770
Instead of throwing Itadori into the fire,
like Gojo does, he gives Itadori the option

00:13:56.770 --> 00:13:58.440
to say no.

00:13:58.440 --> 00:14:03.980
Nanami is a sort of parental figure for Itadori,
that, while strict, gives him a sense of security

00:14:03.980 --> 00:14:05.600
and guidance.

00:14:05.600 --> 00:14:10.040
And most importantly, he gives Yuji a feeling
of achievement and attention by believing

00:14:10.040 --> 00:14:19.720
in him and his abilities.

00:14:19.720 --> 00:14:24.290
In the world of Jujutsu the kids have to risk
their lives while the higher ups pull their

00:14:24.290 --> 00:14:28.110
strings behind the scenes, safely away from
the action, not caring about their suffering

00:14:28.110 --> 00:14:29.110
and pain.

00:14:29.110 --> 00:14:35.290
that’s why nanami keeps saying things like
“being a child is not a sin” and “it’s

00:14:35.290 --> 00:14:43.940
my duty to prioritize your life over mine”
because he's trying to do what the higher-ups

00:14:43.940 --> 00:14:48.490
should have been doing all along, which is
trying to keep these kids Safe and let them

00:14:48.490 --> 00:14:51.310
grow into responsible adults.

00:14:51.310 --> 00:14:55.490
This care for the students and the dislike
of the established structures is one of the

00:14:55.490 --> 00:15:04.650
few things he actually has in common with
Gojo.

00:15:04.650 --> 00:15:09.610
Nanami is an oddity among the sorcery world
not for being an eccentric but for being too

00:15:09.610 --> 00:15:10.610
normal.

00:15:10.610 --> 00:15:12.410
He’s too much of a functioning adult.

00:15:12.410 --> 00:15:18.230
He’s not insane enough like most sorcerers,
which is the case for a goo reason.

00:15:18.230 --> 00:15:27.610
- Gojo explains not everyone can do it - That’s
because Nanami’s number one priority is

00:15:27.610 --> 00:15:32.890
not strength, but rather connecting and cooperating
with others hence why he’s so strong on

00:15:32.890 --> 00:15:33.890
conformism.

00:15:33.890 --> 00:15:37.940
And so, in the end, Nanami’s salaryman-like
serious persona becomes more and more of an

00:15:37.940 --> 00:15:40.010
act as you dwell on his character.

00:15:40.010 --> 00:15:44.360
It’s like he’s putting on a show that
he’s not as mad as everybody else, that

00:15:44.360 --> 00:15:46.970
he’s still reasonable in this world.

00:15:46.970 --> 00:15:51.770
It’s done mostly for his own sake because
Nanami is striving to follow his own ideals

00:15:51.770 --> 00:15:57.180
of being good, in a world he’s well aware
is not so good.

00:15:57.180 --> 00:16:01.399
While being an incredibly sensitive and loving
person at heart, he always forces himself

00:16:01.399 --> 00:16:04.400
to be strict because he believes he has to.

00:16:04.400 --> 00:16:09.550
The moment that best shows this, is during
his fight with Mahito, where he is quite empathic

00:16:09.550 --> 00:16:14.630
to the transfigured humans used by Mahito
in their fight, despite claiming that he doesn’t

00:16:14.630 --> 00:16:26.649
bring his personal feeling to work.

00:16:26.649 --> 00:16:30.890
And it's this fatherly nature of his, the
feeling that there is an adult in the room

00:16:30.890 --> 00:16:36.830
who knows what has to be done, that make Nanami
such a well-respected and dearly loved character.

00:16:36.830 --> 00:16:41.339
And while, despite his best efforts, Nanami
is simply not blessed with the powers of a

00:16:41.339 --> 00:16:47.330
Gojo or Itadori, he is able to pass on his
will and drive to the next generation.

00:16:47.330 --> 00:16:51.660
While he might feel like just another clog
in the system, just like the accumulation

00:16:51.660 --> 00:16:57.690
of little despairs made him grow up, the accumulation
of little acts of kindness are what create

00:16:57.690 --> 00:17:02.490
an impact in the grand scale of things, making
his life worth living.

00:17:02.490 --> 00:17:07.160
Which is why in the face of death, Nanami
is actually able to smile, having lived his

00:17:07.160 --> 00:17:11.770
life suffering, but without regret.

00:17:11.770 --> 00:17:22.050
Now, while Nanami in many ways is a more mature
version of Itadori, having passed his philosophy

00:17:22.050 --> 00:17:27.550
onto him, the student that is actually most
like Gojo, is not Fushiguro, but actually

00:17:27.550 --> 00:17:40.409
Kugisaki Nobora, a refreshingly badass take
on the female support character in shounen.

00:17:40.409 --> 00:17:41.409
-

00:17:41.409 --> 00:17:43.790
Make sure to watch her video by clicking right
here.

00:17:43.790 --> 00:17:45.740
Thanks for watching.

00:17:45.740 --> 00:17:46.390
Peace.

